  "comments": "<p>Three main groups of the Obverse are known.<br><br><i>Obverse</i><br>Die <strong>1</strong> - all details smaller, as the result, circular legend close to the center.<br>Die <strong>2</strong> - all details larger, as the result, circular legend far from the center, dots above \"Ö\" close the letter.<br>Die <strong>3</strong> - circular legend far from the center, dots above \"Ö\" far from the letter.<br>Picture: © Images courtesy of Alexandr Prokofyev.<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/643bbfe1d6fb6.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/643bbfe1d6fb6.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br>Combinations<br>Die <strong>1</strong> - 1967.<br>Die <strong>2</strong> - 1968-1976.<br>Die <strong>3</strong> - 1977-1989.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>2 main obverses of rays touching shield and rays not touching shield on 1989 coins.</p><p><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/677bf2587f468.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/677bf2587f468.jpg\"></a></p>",
